/* book Worked example: Q: A short-wave diathermy unit works at 27.12 MHz. Find the wavelength in air and the period of the wave.
   1. Given f = 27.12 MHz = 27.12 × 10⁶ Hz and c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s.
   2. λ = c ÷ f = (3 × 10⁸ m/s) ÷ (27.12 × 10⁶ Hz) = 11.0619 m ≈ 11.06 m.
   3. T = 1 ÷ f = 1 ÷ (27.12 × 10⁶ Hz) = 3.6873 × 10⁻⁸ s = 36.9 ns.
   4. The 11 m wavelength is far bigger than the limb, so the tissue sits in the near field of the plates and is heated by the field directly. The depth comes from the low absorption per centimetre at this frequency; at 2450 MHz absorption is much higher and the heating stays within a few centimetres.
   Answer: Wavelength λ = 11.06 m and period T = 36.9 ns. */
